// CotSC Batch 18 - extracted original English dialogue for tormha_npcs.d
// Keep existing @ numbers stable when translating.
@1 = ~Howdy, travelers. Want to buy some goods?~
@2 = ~Show us what you got.~
@3 = ~Not right now.~
@4 = ~Not many people visit our village. Being close to Baldur's Gate has its charms but also steals the charm of being a quiet, serendipitous area where you can let your worries dissolve.~
@5 = ~Recently, we had a seer in the village who apparently foretold the future of this village. He said a massive hellcyst will erupt from the ground and swallow the village whole straight into Avernus. Would you believe seers and their party trick lies? Phi.~
@6 = ~Oh, new people in the village? I hope you enjoy your stay... which will be short. Like every other adventurers.~
@7 = ~I'm welcoming you with open arms. What services do you need?~
@8 = ~Who is the leader here?~
@9 = ~What do you know about disappearances in the village?~
@10 = ~What can you tell me about Torm?~
@11 = ~That'll be all.~
@12 = ~Brave adventurers. I am so pleased to see you. Life will go back to normal now and the caves underneath shall be sealed. What can I get you heroes?~
@13 = ~Alma is our grand priestess and overseer. Have you any inquiries or if you came to offer your services and help us find whatever is responsible for disappearing villagers, she's the person to speak to.~
@14 = ~Not more than any other paladin. Speak to Alma. She'll share all details with you.~
@15 = ~Torm is the god of duty, loyalty, and the strength to do what is right, no matter the cost. He demands absolute honesty from his followers and swift judgment for traitors. His symbol is the upright gauntlet—a sign of protection for the weak, and a crushing fist for the wicked.~
@16 = ~As his obedient servants, we ensure to abide by his designated laws and treat them with utmost importance whilst also protecting the innocent. We are dedicated to fighting corruption and preserving righteousness to the best of our ability.~
@17 = ~Any other questions?~
@18 = ~Who is the leader here?~
@19 = ~What do you know about disappearances in the village?~
@20 = ~What can you tell me about Torm?~
@21 = ~That'll be all.~
@22 = ~You're back. How is it going to be?~
@23 = ~We are willing to, Alma. Open the rift for us.~
@24 = ~Do you have any information at all of what we can expect down there?~
@25 = ~We need some time to prepare.~
@26 = ~I'm Alma. Word has spread that new travelers arrived at Torm's Hand. I'll gladly accept your help if you're here to find out about the disappearances.~
@27 = ~We are sent by Randalla Brasshorn. We are tasked with locating her missing agent and solving the problem that plagues the village. What can you tell us about it?~
@28 = ~What happened to Randalla's agent?~
@29 = ~We'll be back.~
@30 = ~Dreadful occurrences have plaqued this village lately. One by one, villagers have gone missing with no apparent assailant responsible for it in sight. Our searches and prayer brought us no luck.~
@31 = ~Reluctantly, I concealed some... information from the villagers, and regrettably the Order. Since you're allied with Randalla I know I can trust you. She has proven herself to me more than once and I am deeply indebted to her and her people. Proceed down the stairs behind the altar, at the back.~
@32 = ~Downstairs, you'll find sleeping quarters and a massive hole leading to a system of caverns running underneath the village. They're unexplored and we have no clue how deep they go. We did not realise all this time what is right beneath our feet. While dressing up in my room downstairs, a few weeks ago I noticed a small crack in the floor that I wasn't aware of before. Right in the middle of my chamber.~
@33 = ~I carefully inspected it and, much to much surprise, uncovered hidden entrance. Upon examination, I discovered fresh footprints leading down, alongside drops of freshly spilled blood. I put the pieces together and concluded that whoever - or whatever - is taking our people, must be down there.~
@34 = ~Alas, there's a catch. These caves are emanating with mystical magical energy which subsequently blocks us from entering, hence why I hadn't informed other paladins. To sent them down there would lead to their ultimate demise. I am capable of creating a temporary rift in this unseen magical barrier that will allow you to enter the depths. I must warn you however, that this is how the last group of adventurers vanished.~
@35 = ~I'm afraid there isn't much else I can do for you. If that's any consolation, you look more skilled and hardened than those last poor souls. I would be grateful for the service and compensate you heavily for your efforts. 8000 gold coins. Deal?~
@36 = ~How is it gonna be?~
@37 = ~We are willing to, Alma. Open the rift for us.~
@38 = ~Do you have any information at all of what we can expect down there?~
@39 = ~We need some time to prepare.~
@40 = ~I will recite an incantation to briefly surpass the magical sphere. You'll enter the caves. Be cautious.~
@41 = ~Had I knew I would've warned you about the threats by now. I do not have the knowledge of literal anything that dwells down the depth.~
@42 = ~Just make haste. People are counting on you. If anyone down there is still alive, we need to hurry.~
@43 = ~Poor soul swore an oath to solve this crisis and vanished two days later. I was just about to sent a troop to inform Randalla when you arrived. I shall sent a paladin on the way later.~
@44 = ~Welcome to the Fortress. Do you need our healing services? Or would you to donate?~
@45 = ~Let's see what you have.~
@46 = ~Nothing right now.~
@47 = ~May Torm bless you.~
